{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"glandulous-minor-aurochs","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\nThe MCP server reviews plan material from its own tickets clone. An edit made in another\nclone (local CLI or library) reaches that clone only through `reads.ensure_fresh`\n(`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`), a best-effort `git fetch` throttled to once per\n60 s by a `/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5>` marker. `collect_plan_relation_snapshot` (review start)\nand the under-lock re-collect in `generation.sign_manifest` both go through that throttle.\n\nSo a review started, or signed, within 60 s of the server's previous fetch can pin a\ndescription that is already superseded on `origin`. The under-lock re-check compares against\nthe same lagging clone, so it does not catch this. A claim through the same server inside the\nsame window would also see the lagging clone.\n\nSplit from next-embattled-geese (3b27-8f4b), which fixes the separate dedup-attach window.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Code path read on origin/main 3beb7e4ad23: `tracker_head_sha` -> `ticket_reads.ensure_fresh`\n  -> throttle check `marker_age < 60: return`.\n- Not yet reproduced end to end; needs two clones sharing one origin.\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\nBypass the throttle (forced fetch + reconverge) for the gate's own material reads at review\nstart and before taking the signing lock, without fetching while the store lock is held.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two-clone test: edit in clone A and push; within 60 s of clone B's last fetch, a review\n  started on B pins A's edited description.\n- [ ] Signing on B refuses when A's edit lands on origin during the run.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit -k cross_clone_freshness -q\n```","id":"36d1-9578-d4b3-48c9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP plan review can read and sign a tickets clone up to 60 s behind origin after a cross-clone edit"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792371123039919817,"uuid":"a9cf0eda-17b0-4af2-8982-b6f97d832a9a"}